# fixedbugs, defect 2049, 2026-10-13, a call inside a call.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own writing
# `hero_print_int(hero_str_len(8))` was told `internal error: compiling
# the generated C failed` at exit 2, as the third reproducer was.
#
# FIX: the note is told as the runtime's `hero_str_len`, the call
# whose parentheses hold clang's caret, never the call around it
# (`cli/runtime_name.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2049-a-header-that-calls-a-runtime-function-inside-another-call-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
